        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Monfragüe, Doñana National Park, Andalusia, Huelva, Seville\n- Organizations: World Wildlife Fund, Spanish government\n- Water bodies: Tiétar, Tagus\n- Topics: national parks, nature reserves, bird-life\n\nFacts:\n- In 1969, Doñana National Park was established as a nature reserve when the World Wildlife Fund joined with the Spanish government and purchased a section of marshes to protect it.\n- Monfragüe is a Spanish national park noted for its bird-life.\n- Doñana National Park is a natural reserve in Andalusia in southern Spain, located in the provinces of Huelva and Seville.\n- The Tiétar River flows into the Tagus at Monfragüe.",
